<newsitem itemid="56981" id="root" date="1996-09-16" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Adwest slides to full-year loss.</title>
<headline>Adwest slides to full-year loss.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		30.7 loss	    vs 12.5 profit</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.5		    vs 5.5</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 7.8		    vs 7.8</p>
<p> Pretax		     23.0 loss	    vs 14.8 million profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   223.6		  vs 201.5</p>
<p>NOTE - The automotive components and electronics group said its results were hit by a nine million stg provision for losses on its disposal programme, 20.2 million stg for write-down of goodwill and another five million stg of exceptional charges.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 10.0		   vs 16.2</p>
<p> Exceptional		5.0		    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest (payable)     3.9		    vs 2.0</p>
<p> Tax			  2.1		    vs 4.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		  25.1 loss	    vs 10.3 profit</p>
<p> Retained		   25.3 loss	    vs 3.8 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 22</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 8</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said the current financial year has started well with order books and profits ahead of last year.</p>
</text>
